# Athlete Profile

This file stores your personal goals, preferences, and physical parameters. The AI coach uses it as context for every conversation.

**Setup:** Ask the AI to "run the onboarding flow" and it will pull data from your Garmin account, walk you through the rest (including **confirming your time zone**), and update this file automatically. Or fill in the sections below manually.

Sections marked with `AUTO` can be populated from Garmin data. Sections marked with `YOU` need your input.

## Athlete Info `AUTO`

Auto-populated from `get_user_profile`. Confirm during onboarding.

- **Gender:** (auto)
- **Birthday:** (auto)
- **Height:** (auto, cm)
- **Weight:** (auto, kg)
- **Measurement system:** (auto, metric/imperial)

## Time zone `AUTO` + `YOU`

Garmin Connect uses an account **time zone** for calendars, scheduling, and how some dates are interpreted. It may differ from where you actually train or your watch’s “home” location.

- **Default time zone (IANA):** (auto from `get_userprofile_settings` → `timeZone`, e.g. `Australia/Sydney`, `Europe/Stockholm`)
- **Confirmed for coaching:** `YOU` — During **onboarding**, the AI must **show the auto value** and ask you to **confirm or correct** it. If Connect is wrong, update Connect **or** store the canonical zone here for chat (scheduling, “today”, weekly plan context). Always use a valid **IANA** name (e.g. `America/New_York`), not a numeric offset alone.

> **Tip:** This value helps reason about `schedule_workout` calendar dates vs the day you see in Connect (see `workout-handling.mdc`).

## Race Calendar `YOU`

List your upcoming races. The AI uses these to determine your current training block phase automatically (base → build → peak → taper) and to periodise your training around the primary race.

### Primary Race (A race)

- **Race:** (e.g., Stockholm Half Marathon)
- **Distance:** (e.g., half marathon or 21.1 km)
- **Date:** (e.g., 2026-05-17)
- **Goal time:** (e.g., sub-1:45)

### Secondary Races (B/C races)

These are training races, tune-ups, or lower-priority events. The AI will fit them into the plan without compromising primary race preparation.

- (e.g., B — Parkrun 5K, 2026-04-04, use as threshold test)
- (e.g., C — Local 10K, 2026-04-19, race effort but not tapered)

> **Tip:** Goals and races are separate in Garmin Connect. The Garmin MCP has no tool for planned races — `get_goals` returns only goals (e.g. distance targets), not race events. This Race Calendar is the primary source the AI uses for periodisation. Keep it updated when you add or change races.

## Training Availability `AUTO` + `YOU`

Available training days and preferred long run day can be auto-populated from `get_user_profile` (`availableTrainingDays`, `preferredLongTrainingDays`). Quality session days and time constraints need your input.

- **Running days per week:** (auto/confirm)
- **Available days:** (auto from Garmin, confirm)
- **Long run day:** (auto from Garmin, confirm)
- **Quality session days:** `YOU` (e.g., Tuesday, Thursday)
- **Time constraints:** `YOU` (e.g., weekday runs max 60 min, weekends flexible)

## Heart Rate, Pace & Power Zones `AUTO` + `YOU`

All values below are auto-populated from Garmin. The AI should refresh these periodically — Garmin updates them dynamically from activity data when auto-detect is enabled.

**Live zones vs this file:** Zone **bpm ranges** follow what is configured in **Garmin Connect** and on the **watch**; they can **change week to week** (manual edits, sync, auto-detect threshold updates, or zone-method changes). For **weekly plans and HR-targeted workouts**, the coach must **re-fetch** zone definitions from Garmin for that session (`get_user_profile`, `get_userprofile_settings`, `get_lactate_threshold` as in `training-plans.mdc`). Treat the **Zones** table below as **reference / last-known snapshot**, not the source of truth until refreshed.

**Data retrieval priority:**

1. Pull running-specific metrics from `get_user_profile` → `userData` (contains `lactateThresholdHeartRate`, `lactateThresholdSpeed`, `vo2MaxRunning`; parse any **HR zone** fields returned in the same payload).
2. Pull detailed threshold data from `get_lactate_threshold` (includes FTP, staleness indicator).
3. Pull resting HR from `get_rhr_day`.
4. Use `get_userprofile_settings` when zone or HR settings are surfaced there and not complete in `get_user_profile`.
5. If running-specific values are missing, fall back to generic profile values.

> **Max HR** is set in Garmin Connect (either from Garmin's own formula or manually by the athlete). The current MCP tools may not expose it directly — if not available, ask the athlete to provide it during onboarding. Do NOT estimate max HR from recent activity data.

- **Max HR:** `YOU` (from Garmin profile or manual entry, e.g., 185 bpm)
- **Resting HR:** (auto, e.g., 38 bpm)
- **VO2max:** (auto, e.g., 50)
- **LTHR (Lactate Threshold HR):** (auto, e.g., 162 bpm)
- **Lactate threshold pace:** (auto, e.g., 4:41/km)
- **FTP (running power):** (auto, e.g., 379 W)
- **Zone method:** (auto from Garmin config, or ask athlete: %LTHR / %MaxHR / %HRR)
- **Use HR-based targets** `YOU` for: easy runs, threshold sessions, aerobic runs, recovery runs, long runs
- **Use pace-based targets** `YOU`for: race pace work, long and short intervals
- **Use power-based targets** `YOU`for: hill repeats, sprint intervals

### Zones

Default zone boundaries use %LTHR, matching Garmin Connect defaults. Recommended zone method in order of preference: **%LTHR → %HRR → %MaxHR**.

| Zone | Name      | %LTHR    | Description                        |
| ---- | --------- | -------- | ---------------------------------- |
| 5    | Maximum   | 100–107% | Max effort, short intervals only   |
| 4    | Threshold | 95–99%   | Hard, sustainable ~20–30 min       |
| 3    | Aerobic   | 89–94%   | Comfortably hard, sustained tempo  |
| 2    | Easy      | 80–88%   | Easy/conversational, base building |
| 1    | Warm Up   | 65–79%   | Very easy, warm-up and cool-down   |

> **Note:** When LTHR or zones feel outdated, ask the AI to refresh them from Garmin. If auto-detect is enabled on your device, these update after qualifying activities. Even when this file is up to date, the coach still pulls **current** Connect zones again before each **weekly plan** so prescriptions match the watch.

